            <ArticleTitle>An unusual complication of interscalene brachial plexus catheterization: delayed catheter migration.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>535-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case report describes the delayed migration of an interscalene brachial plexus catheter that was inserted for postoperative analgesia and to facilitate physiotherapy after shoulder surgery. Approximately 18 h after surgery the catheter was found to have migrated into the interpleural space, which could have resulted in a serious complication, namely a pneumothorax.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
